```

**Autocast wrapper for an autograd-enabled op** — just register on the same name; no separate backward gymnastics needed. The backward method runs in the same dtype autocast sets for forward, so choose a `<desired dtype>` suitable for both:

```cpp
Tensor myadd_autocast(const Tensor& self, const Tensor& other) {
  c10::impl::ExcludeDispatchKeyGuard no_autocast(c10::DispatchKey::Autocast);
  return myadd(at::autocast::cached_cast(<desired dtype>, self),
               at::autocast::cached_cast(<desired dtype>, other));
}

TORCH_LIBRARY_IMPL(myops, Autocast, m) {
  m.impl("myadd", myadd_autocast);
}
```

#### Batched

Batched tensors allow per-example code that is automatically batched under `vmap`. The batching-rules API is **currently under development**; once stabilized, register a kernel at the `Batched` dispatch key.

#### Tracer

The `Tracer` dispatch key supports recording operator invocations into a trace under `torch.jit.trace`. A boxed fallback for tracing arbitrary operations is **intended but not yet provided** — track progress at issue #41478.

---

## Summary Checklist

